    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d689">

                <pb facs="0843" n="749" xml:id="pg749"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">823.01/12: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor of Embassy in Peru</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Mayer</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-09-11T10:00:00-05:00">September 11, 1930—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 12:35 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>202. My 201, September 10, 8 p.m. Paraguay has accorded recognition; and I
                    understand the British Chargé d’Affaires, French Minister, and Papal Nuncio have
                    recommended to their respective Governments that recognition be given. The
                    German Minister may do the same.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mayer</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
